# NOBA Archive - what never enters version control.
#
# The rule this file follows: a thing belongs in the repository when it is SOURCE - something a
# person wrote, that cannot be regenerated from what is already here. Everything else is either
# output (regenerate it), private (it is not the project's to publish), or enormous (it makes every
# future clone pay for a decision made once).
#
# Git history is permanent. A file deleted in a later commit is still in the history, still cloned,
# and still readable. So the first commit is the only cheap place to get this right.

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
TestResults/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.idea/
x64/
x86/
Debug/
Release/
*.tlog
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.exp
*.ilk

# The native adapter's MSVC output, which lands beside its sources rather than under bin/.
src/NOBA.Archive.ShellAdapter/x64/

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packaging, signing, deployment
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A sparse package and everything used to sign it. The DEV-ONLY certificate is regenerated by
# scripts\dev-certificate.ps1 in one command, and a signing key is not a thing to keep beside code
# even when it is public and even when it is called DEV-ONLY.
*.msix
*.msixbundle
*.appx
*.appxbundle
*.pfx
*.cer
*.snk
*.p12

# NOT AppxManifest.xml as a blanket rule. The GENERATED manifest lives under artifacts\sparse-stage
# and is already excluded with the rest of artifacts/. Two hand-written manifests are SOURCE -
# packaging\sparse\AppxManifest.xml and harness\phase5-e\package\AppxManifest.xml - and a rule by
# filename alone would silently drop both. The first draft of this file did exactly that.

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated fixtures
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 17 MB of deliberately incompressible bytes, built by scripts\make-ops-fixture.ps1 and documented
# in fixtures\README.md. Committing it would put 17 MB of random data in every clone forever to save
# one command. The README stays; the archive does not.
fixtures/noba-ops.7z

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT THE PROJECT'S TO PUBLISH
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rar/ holds personal and work archives that were used as ad-hoc test input - engineering drawings,
# invoices, files dating back to 2008. They are the owner's documents, not project fixtures, and
# they are about 107 MB. Test input that matters belongs in fixtures/ with a README explaining what
# it proves.
rar/
test.7z
*.docx
noba-archive-phase1-source.zip
noba-archive-phase2-source.zip
noba-archive-phase2-source/
NOBA_Archive_Brand_FINAL_LOCKED*/

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ad-hoc archives anywhere in the tree
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately broad. An archive manager's working directory collects test archives constantly, and
# one committed by accident is permanent. Anything that genuinely belongs in the repository can be
# added explicitly with `git add -f`, which is a decision somebody made on purpose.
*.7z
*.rar
*.zip
*.tar
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.cab
*.iso

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local noise
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# MSVC / harness outputs compiled beside their sources
*.obj
*.exe
*.dll
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.res

# Phase-5 harness staging and results
harness/**/stage/
harness/**/results/
harness/**/build/
artifacts/sparse-stage/

# Explorer scratch folders
fixtures/New folder*/
